# Kriko .gitignore, grouped by who makes the file.
# Rule of thumb: a source is committed; anything a command regenerates is not.
# Check after editing: `git ls-files -ci --exclude-standard` must print nothing
# (a tracked file that is also ignored is a rule that lies).

# --- Python ----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.venv-*/
venv/
src/*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- Node ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Lockfiles are committed on purpose, at every depth. A bare
# `package-lock.json` rule once swallowed the root one, a dependency floated,
# and a byte-identical tree built an app that panicked. A release that cannot
# be rebuilt is not a release.
node_modules/

# --- Build output (each one regenerated by its own command) -----------------
# dist/: packs (`kriko build`) and the frozen sidecar (packaging/freeze.sh).
dist/
build/
build.log
# The desktop app. package.ps1 builds its release tree outside the checkout
# (%LOCALAPPDATA%\Kriko\cargo-target), so this glob is for a plain `cargo build`
# or `tauri dev` run from a checkout, which still writes kriko-ui/src-tauri/target
# (about 2 GB per worktree or agent, hence the glob). Installers come from
# kriko-ui/package.ps1.
kriko-ui/src-tauri/target*/
kriko-ui/src-tauri/binaries/
kriko-ui/node_modules/
kriko-ui/dist/
kriko-ui/builds/

# --- Build tools kept beside the checkout ----------------------------------
# The WiX 3 toolset the MSI recipe used. Nothing needs it since the NSIS installer;
# a copy left in a checkout stays ignored.
tools/wix314/

# --- The mobile app (kriko-mobile/) ----------------------------------------
# Expo and Metro write these; `npx expo start` regenerates them.
kriko-mobile/.expo/
kriko-mobile/dist/
kriko-mobile/expo-env.d.ts

# Design scratch, each regenerated by the tool that made it:
#   .fonts/   the Archivo variable source, downloaded by tools/make_fonts.py
#   .preview/ the design captures, our emulator screenshots, compare sheets
.fonts/
.preview/

# --- Runtime data the engine and pipelines write ---------------------------
# Evidence ledger (src/kriko/ledger/db.py) and the per-pack pipeline caches.
src/kriko/ledger.db
packs/*/pipeline/ledger_export/
packs/*/pipeline/cache/
logs/
.cache/

# pip's and pytest's own scratch directories, when they land in the working
# directory instead of the system temp folder (which is what happens when TMPDIR
# is unset or points somewhere unwritable). Ten of each were sitting untracked in
# this checkout when the sweep was written, and `git status` was unusable
# because of it.
pip-build-tracker-*/
pip-ephem-wheel-cache-*/
pip-install-*/
pip-uninstall-*/
pytest-of-*/
pytest-*/
# And the same for a test that makes its own scratch directory through
# `tempfile.mkdtemp()` when the system temp folder is unusable: two of these
# (`tmp405ayqt4`, `tmpdeq23wol`, each with a real app.sqlite in it) were left in
# the checkout by a suite run and showed up as untracked files.
tmp?????????/

# --- Secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Editors, agents and local tools ---------------------------------------
# Agent tool folders. Each holds local state, and the one research-agent file
# in each is generated by packs/<name>/pipeline/agent/render.py on the machine
# that uses it, so neither is source.
.claude/
.opencode/
.zed/
.delta/
.review/
.walk/
.superpowers/

# --- Isolated work ---------------------------------------------------------
# A git worktree made for isolated work. Not source: it holds its own checkout
# of the same tree, so committing it would commit the tree twice.
.worktrees/

# --- Build tools kept beside the checkout ----------------------------------

# --- Scratch ---------------------------------------------------------------
# A review session's own working files: a captured PNG, an engine log, a seed
# script. Regenerated on demand, never source.
.tmp-*
_c.png
_crop.png

# Local task backups and evaluation scratch
.local-evaluation/

# Something in this working tree drops files with non-UTF-8 names (an imgui
# layout, by its contents). Six were once committed and made `git checkout`
# fail on Windows and macOS (see
# test_every_tracked_path_is_checkoutable_on_windows_and_macos). Ignored by
# their literal bytes so no `git add -A` can pick one up again. Keep this the
# last line, and edit this file with a byte-safe tool.
0�d
release/
dl/

# --- The relay (server/) ----------------------------------------------------
server/.env
server/*.sqlite*
server/*.key

# --- Shared access (src/app/sharekeys.py) -----------------------------------
# The build pepper and the trial bundle ARE credentials: whoever holds the
# pepper can open an access code without the app that sealed it, and whoever
# holds the trial bundle can spend the key it carries. Written by
# `tools/make_share_pepper.py` and `tools/make_trial_access.py`, on the machine
# that makes the release, and never committed.
src/app/sharekeys_pepper.py
src/app/trial_access.json

# Local scratch and artifacts that are not part of the product.
.dsh-tmp/
.vscode/
kriko-gpui/
logs.txt
pytest-run.log

# --- the advertisement ------------------------------------------------------
# Frames and the rendered video are made by `site/tools/ad/render.mjs`.
site/tools/ad/out/
